# D112: a secure connection to something that does not speak TLS fails its
# handshake, and the failure reaches "on error of". All on loopback.
listen for tcp on port 0 and call it server
on connection to server
    conn is incoming connection
    on data from conn
        send bytes from text "this is not TLS" through conn
        close tcp conn
    .
.
connect securely to tcp "127.0.0.1" on port local port of server for server "localhost" and call it secure
say "state:" state of secure
on connect of secure
    say "connected, which should not happen"
.
on error of secure
    if network error starts with "The TLS handshake with 127.0.0.1 failed: "
        say "the handshake failed"
    .
    say "state:" state of secure
    if not secure is secure
        say "the connection is not secure"
    .
    stop tcp server
.
